<title>USA: Allstate forms emergency roadside help unit.</title>
<headline>Allstate forms emergency roadside help unit.</headline>
<dateline>NORTHBROOK, Ill. 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Allstate Insurance Co, an Allstate Corp subsidiary, said it formed Rescue Express Inc, a nationwide network of emergency roadside assistance franchises.</p>
<p>Initially, the service has targeted several states and cities throughout the country for franchise development.</p>
<p>Rescue Express franchises consist of a fleet of 24-hour-a-day service vehicles linked via a setellite tracking system.</p>
<p>((Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
